 "inference": [
  "The scale transfers by profile equality, not observation, to 63 of 67 weapons. Measured profiles are all decExp 1; the 70/0.6/4 profile (9 weapons) differs in law form and is unmeasured.",
  "The scale has no site effect on the seven bolt rifles (residual 0 at the bolt cycle under 0.8 and 1.0) but moves pump shotgun sustained fire by 22 to 66% at shot 3 to 11.",
  "No existing clip constrains the scale off the four measured weapons; the DB-12 633 ms pump pauses lean toward 0.8 but are not usable as a constraint."
 ],
 "unresolved": [
  "The 0.8 scale is not measured on any sniper, pump or semi shotgun, sidearm, SMG or LMG; transfer within identical profiles rests on equality of (factor, exponent, time exponent, offset), not on observation.",
  "The 70/0.6/4 profile (decExp 0.6) is the one profile with a different law form; whether the scale transfers to it is open. It matters only for M87A1 and DB-12 sustained pump fire.",
  "DB-12 633 ms pump-pause aim climbs (+0.20, -0.23 deg clean; -3.09 contaminated) lean toward x0.8 (+0.038) over x1.0 (-0.471) but carry no error estimate and include mouse input; no re-track was attempted (no new fits).",
  "KS-18K 417 ms interval: measured climb 1.55 deg up against a predicted fall of 0.26 (x0.8) or 0.47 (x1.0); contradicts both and is unexplained. Not investigated.",
  "The M87A1 pump capture is conditional: rule (2) requires asking the operator before any recording is requested.",
  "The brief says no DMR was measured; data/weapons.json classes LMR27 as DMR. The class rows follow the data.",
  "Raw EBX not read (site-only lead); no rawChecks apply."
 ],
 "siteImpact": "No site change from this lead. Conditional: if the operator accepts the M87A1 pump capture and the 633 ms pair separation lands near 1.21 deg (x1.0) rather than 1.57 deg (x0.8), the 70/0.6/4 profile (M87A1, DB-12) takes its own recovery scale, replacing the single constant with a per-profile table; M87A1 sustained-fire pre-shot aim at shot 11 would fall from 4.76 to 2.87 deg and DB-12 from 7.87 to 5.55 deg. Snipers are unchanged either way. Until then the global 0.8 stands: measured on Assault Rifle (TR-7, M433), Carbine (AK-205) and DMR (LMR27), transferred to the other 63 weapons.",
